PRIVATELY ATTACK CHAINS =E2=80=94 DEFENSIVE SYNTHESIS

1 NEW ATTACK CHAINS

AC-2026-PLUGIN-PIN-IDENTITY-CONFUSION =E2=80=94 RECENT / PARTIALLY PATCHED

Aliases: Plugin4Shell; plugin SHA-pin bypass; reviewed-plugin rug-pull.

Canonical fingerprint: trusted/reviewed plugin -> marketplace pins
immutable-looking commit identity -> upstream repository authority
changes resolution semantics -> agent background update resolves pin
to different code -> plugin executes with developer/agent authority ->
secrets/cloud/CI/signer access UNKNOWN -> consequential external
action UNKNOWN.

Evidence: AIR Security disclosed Plugin4Shell on 17 Sep 2026 after
coordinated disclosure. Their research demonstrates the same
distribution-layer design failure across Claude Code, Codex, GitHub
Copilot and Gemini CLI. The agent requests a pinned revision but fails
to verify that the resulting working tree HEAD equals the intended
immutable commit. In affected configurations, attacker-controlled
repository refs can therefore cause different code to install while
the marketplace=E2=80=99s reviewed pin remains unchanged. Claude Code 2.1.1=
79
and Codex 0.146.0 are reported patched; AIR reports no Copilot fix and
says deprecated Gemini CLI will not receive one.

Stages/edges:

ENTRY: already-installed trusted plugin or previously reviewed plugin
[CONFIRMED/T1]

-> upstream repository under attacker/maintainer control [CONFIRMED
prerequisite/T1]

-> immutable-looking marketplace pin [CONFIRMED/T1]

-> repository resolution ambiguity/substitution [CONFIRMED/T1]

-> background plugin update [CONFIRMED for affected auto-update paths/T1]

-> different working tree than reviewed commit [CONFIRMED/T1]

-> plugin code execution on developer host [CONFIRMED lab/T1]

-> credential/session access [UNKNOWN in a documented hostile incident]

-> cloud/CI/signer authority [UNKNOWN]

-> external privileged action [UNKNOWN].

Status: RECENT; LAB-VALIDATED; patch status product-dependent. No
confirmed hostile exploitation established by the disclosure.

2 MATERIAL CHAIN UPDATES

None crossing threshold this hour. Latest Incident Intake at 03:58
reported NO MATERIAL DELTA. No Sent-mail Repo Forensics report was
found. Latest Scanner at 03:48 was recovered as state input.

3 TOP RECURRING SECOND-ORDER MECHANISMS

- Authority-object identity confusion: a security policy approves
identifier X but execution resolves X to mutable/different object Y.

- Delegated capability as credential: module/plugin/agent authority
can be sufficient without stealing an owner key.

- Trust-order inversion: repository/plugin configuration is evaluated
before or outside intended approval boundaries.

- Persistent authority after credential rotation: delegated
owner/publisher/session relationships can outlive the credential that
created them.

- Compositional authorization failure: individually valid
read/write/tool grants compose into an unauthorized flow.

4 STAGE/EDGE GRAPH

reviewed plugin [C/T1] -> pinned revision [C/T1] -> upstream repo
control [C prerequisite/T1] -> resolution substitution [C/T1] ->
background update [C/T1] -> unreviewed code executes [C lab/T1] ->
secret/session [UNKNOWN] -> cloud/CI/signer [UNKNOWN] -> external
action [UNKNOWN].

5 UNKNOWN LINKS WORTH RESOLVING

Highest information gain: public telemetry showing Plugin4Shell-like
distribution substitution followed by actual credential access or
authenticated downstream action. Do not infer those edges from host
RCE alone.

6 DEFENSIVE CHOKEPOINTS + DETECTION

- Verify the resolved immutable object after checkout/install, not
merely the requested ref.

- Record requested plugin identity and resolved content digest as
separate audit fields.

- Fail closed on mismatch/ambiguous refs.

- Disable or gate background plugin updates where provenance cannot be
re-attested.

- Treat plugin execution authority independently from marketplace review st=
atus.

- Alert when an installed plugin=E2=80=99s resolved digest changes without =
a
corresponding approved manifest transition.

- Constrain plugin host access to secrets, CI tokens and signing material.

QP implication: ALLOW(plugin P@digest D) must bind authorization to
the resolved content object D. request(D) is not evidence that
execute(D) occurred.

7 SAFE LAB REPRODUCTION QUEUE

Use a disposable local Git service, harmless plugin and benign marker
action. Model an identifier-resolution collision and verify that a
corrected installer rejects any checkout whose resolved digest differs
from the approved digest. No real credentials, third-party
repositories or production agents.

8 CROSS-CASE CLUSTERS

Cluster: IDENTITY-TO-AUTHORITY BINDING FAILURE.

Members now include Plugin4Shell (requested revision !=3D executed
revision), shared-cache credential crossover (authenticated identity
!=3D credential recipient), inference-router substitution (nominal
provider !=3D actual upstream), and delegated-module authority (approved
module !=3D approved composed action). Common invariant: security
decision is made over one object/identity while authority is exercised
by another.

